  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="page-hero">

    <div class="hero-content">

      <div class="eyebrow">
        Academic Excellence
      </div>

      <h1>
        Learning With Purpose
      </h1>

      <p>
        A structured and engaging educational journey designed to help
        students build knowledge, confidence, critical thinking and
        the skills needed for the future.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>

  <!-- ACADEMIC OVERVIEW -->
  <section class="section overview">

    <div class="overview-grid">

      <div class="overview-text">

        <div class="eyebrow">
          Our Academic Approach
        </div>

        <h2>
          Education That Develops the Whole Learner
        </h2>

        <p>
          At Crestfield International Academy, academic development
          combines strong subject knowledge with curiosity, creativity,
          communication and independent thinking.
        </p>

        <p>
          Students are encouraged to understand what they learn,
          apply knowledge to real situations and develop the confidence
          to ask questions and explore new ideas.
        </p>

        <p>
          Our academic structure is designed to provide continuity
          as learners progress from their earliest years through
          secondary education.
        </p>

      </div>

      <div class="overview-image">

        <img
          src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1503676260728-1c00da094a0b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1000&q=85"
          alt="Students learning in a classroom">

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>

  <!-- ACADEMIC LEVELS -->
  <section class="levels">

    <div class="section">

      <div class="section-heading center">

        <div class="eyebrow">
          Academic Pathways
        </div>

        <h2>
          Learning Across Every Stage
        </h2>

        <p>
          Our academic pathways are structured around the changing
          needs and developmental stages of learners.
        </p>

      </div>

      <div class="levels-grid">

        <!-- EARLY YEARS -->
        <div class="level-card">

          <div class="level-number">
            01 — EARLY YEARS
          </div>

          <h3>
            Early Years Programme
          </h3>

          <p>
            A nurturing foundation where young learners begin developing
            communication, social, creative, numerical and problem-solving
            skills through purposeful learning experiences.
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>Early literacy and communication</li>
            <li>Numeracy foundations</li>
            <li>Creative exploration</li>
            <li>Social development</li>
          </ul>

        </div>

        <!-- PRIMARY -->
        <div class="level-card">

          <div class="level-number">
            02 — PRIMARY
          </div>

          <h3>
            Primary School
          </h3>

          <p>
            Students build strong foundations across core subjects
            while developing curiosity, confidence, study habits
            and independent learning skills.
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>Core academic subjects</li>
            <li>Reading and writing development</li>
            <li>Mathematical reasoning</li>
            <li>Creative and practical learning</li>
          </ul>

        </div>

        <!-- JUNIOR SECONDARY -->
        <div class="level-card">

          <div class="level-number">
            03 — JUNIOR SECONDARY
          </div>

          <h3>
            Junior Secondary School
          </h3>

          <p>
            Learners encounter broader subject areas and increasingly
            challenging concepts while developing analytical thinking
            and greater academic independence.
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>Expanded subject learning</li>
            <li>Research and inquiry</li>
            <li>Problem-solving</li>
            <li>Independent study skills</li>
          </ul>

        </div>

        <!-- SENIOR SECONDARY -->
        <div class="level-card">

          <div class="level-number">
            04 — SENIOR SECONDARY
          </div>

          <h3>
            Senior Secondary School
          </h3>

          <p>
            Students prepare for advanced academic study and future
            pathways while strengthening subject knowledge, critical
            thinking, communication and examination readiness.
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>Advanced subject development</li>
            <li>Examination preparation</li>
            <li>Career awareness</li>
            <li>University and future readiness</li>
          </ul>

        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>

  <!-- CURRICULUM -->
  <section class="curriculum">

    <div class="section">

      <div class="section-heading">

        <div class="eyebrow">
          Curriculum
        </div>

        <h2>
          Broad Knowledge. Strong Foundations.
        </h2>

        <p>
          The curriculum is presented as a balanced learning framework
          that encourages students to build knowledge while developing
          transferable skills.
        </p>

      </div>

      <div class="curriculum-grid">

        <div class="curriculum-card">

          <h3>
            Languages & Communication
          </h3>

          <p>
            Students develop reading, writing, speaking, listening
            and communication skills that support learning across
            different subjects.
          </p>

        </div>

        <div class="curriculum-card">

          <h3>
            Mathematics & Reasoning
          </h3>

          <p>
            Mathematical thinking is developed through structured
            learning, reasoning, problem-solving and practical
            application.
          </p>

        </div>

        <div class="curriculum-card">

          <h3>
            Science & Discovery
          </h3>

          <p>
            Learners explore scientific ideas through observation,
            questioning, investigation and evidence-based thinking.
          </p>

        </div>

        <div class="curriculum-card">

          <h3>
            Humanities & Society
          </h3>

          <p>
            Students explore people, communities, history, geography,
            culture and the world around them.
          </p>

        </div>

        <div class="curriculum-card">

          <h3>
            Technology & Digital Skills
          </h3>

          <p>
            Digital learning supports research, communication,
            creativity and responsible use of technology.
          </p>

        </div>

        <div class="curriculum-card">

          <h3>
            Creative Development
          </h3>

          <p>
            Creative activities provide opportunities for students
            to express ideas, experiment and develop imagination.
          </p>

        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>

  <!-- TEACHING APPROACH -->
  <section class="teaching">

    <div class="section">

      <div class="section-heading center">

        <div class="eyebrow">
          Teaching & Learning
        </div>

        <h2>
          How We Support Learning
        </h2>

        <p>
          Effective learning requires more than delivering information.
          Our approach encourages participation, understanding and application.
        </p>

      </div>

      <div class="teaching-grid">

        <div class="teaching-card">

          <h3>
            Interactive Lessons
          </h3>

          <p>
            Students are encouraged to participate in discussions,
            activities, questions and practical learning experiences.
          </p>

        </div>

        <div class="teaching-card">

          <h3>
            Critical Thinking
          </h3>

          <p>
            Learners are encouraged to examine ideas, ask questions,
            compare information and develop reasoned conclusions.
          </p>

        </div>

        <div class="teaching-card">

          <h3>
            Practical Application
          </h3>

          <p>
            Where appropriate, learning connects classroom knowledge
            with practical examples, projects and real-world situations.
          </p>

        </div>

        <div class="teaching-card">

          <h3>
            Collaboration
          </h3>

          <p>
            Group activities help students practise communication,
            cooperation, listening and shared problem-solving.
          </p>

        </div>

        <div class="teaching-card">

          <h3>
            Independent Learning
          </h3>

          <p>
            Students gradually develop research, organisation and
            study habits that encourage greater ownership of learning.
          </p>

        </div>

        <div class="teaching-card">

          <h3>
            Continuous Feedback
          </h3>

          <p>
            Feedback helps learners understand their progress,
            identify areas for improvement and set meaningful goals.
          </p>

        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>

  <!-- ASSESSMENT -->
  <section class="section">

    <div class="assessment-grid">

      <div class="assessment-text">

        <div class="eyebrow">
          Assessment
        </div>

        <h2>
          Measuring Progress, Guiding Improvement
        </h2>

        <p>
          Assessment provides teachers and learners with useful
          information about academic progress.
        </p>

        <p>
